v32-4.display:
God—true are His works,
and all His ways are judgments;
a faithful God, and there is no unrighteousness;
righteous and holy is the Lord.

v32-7.display:
Remember the days of old;
consider the years of generation upon generation.
Ask your father, and he shall declare unto you;
your elders, and they shall tell you.

v32-15.display:
And Jacob ate and was filled,
and the beloved one kicked;
he grew fat, he grew thick, he grew broad;
and he forsook God who made him,
and departed from God his Saviour.

v32-20.display:
And He said, I will turn My face from them,
and show what shall befall them at the last;
for they are a perverse generation,
sons in whom is no faithfulness.

v32-21.display:
They made Me jealous with that which is no god;
they provoked Me to anger with their idols.
And I will make them jealous with that which is no nation;
with a nation without understanding will I provoke them to anger.

v32-35.display:
In the day of vengeance I will repay,
in the season when their foot shall slip;
for the day of their destruction is near,
and the things prepared for you are at hand.

v32-36.display:
For the Lord shall judge His people,
and be moved concerning His servants;
for He saw them weakened,
and failing under assault, and exhausted.

v32-39.display:
See, see that I am,
and there is no god beside Me.
I will put to death, and make alive;
I will smite, and I will heal;
and there is none that shall deliver out of My hands.

v32-43.display:
Rejoice, O heavens, together with Him,
and let all the sons of God worship Him;
rejoice, O nations, with His people,
and let all the angels of God give Him strength;
for He avenges the blood of His sons,
and shall avenge and repay a penalty unto the enemies,
and unto them that hate Him shall He repay;
and the Lord shall thoroughly cleanse the land of His people.

v33-3.display:
And He spared His people;
and all the consecrated ones are under Thy hands;
and these are under Thee;
and the people received from His words

v33-17.display:
His beauty is that of a firstborn bull;
his horns are the horns of a one-horned animal;
with them shall he gore the nations together unto the end of the earth.
These are the myriads of Ephraim,
and these are the thousands of Manasseh.

v33-18.display:
And unto Zebulun he said,
Rejoice, Zebulun, in your going forth;
and Issachar, in his dwellings.

v33-19.display:
They shall destroy nations;
and you shall call upon God there,
and sacrifice a sacrifice of righteousness;
for the wealth of the sea shall nourish you,
and the commerce of them that dwell by the coast.

v33-23.display:
And unto Naphtali he said,
Naphtali, a fullness of acceptable things;
and let him be filled with blessing from the Lord;
he shall inherit the sea and the south.
